## Run

```bash
npm install          # or pnpm install
cp .env.example .env
npm run migrate      # create the schema
npm run dev          # start on http://localhost:4000
```

## Layout

```
src/
  server.ts            # entry point — YOURS to extend (written once, never overwritten)
  generated/           # owned by Backbone — regenerated wholesale, do not edit
    config/            # env + knex instance
    middleware/        # error handler<% if (auth) { %> + JWT auth guard<% } %>
    models/            # repositories over Knex
    services/          # business layer
    controllers/       # Express handlers
    validators/        # zod request schemas
    routes/            # per-entity routers + index
<% if (auth) { %>    auth/              # register / login / me
<% } %>    types.ts           # entity interfaces
migrations/            # additive, timestamped — never edited or deleted
scripts/migrate.ts     # runs knex migrate:latest
```

Anything under `src/generated/` is overwritten every time you regenerate. Everything else is
yours. Add custom routes in `src/server.ts` where marked.

